WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.503
-Guys, today is Thursday.
-Right.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.039
-And that's usually when I catch
up on some personal stuff.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.374
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.476
You know, normally
it would be Friday.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:11.644
-Yeah. I mean, it's Thursday.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.680
-No.
This is the way it works now.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.314
-Oh.
-Thursday is the new Friday.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:16.816
-Oh.
-You know what I'm saying?

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.017
This is like --
-Yeah.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:21.287
-The weekend longer.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.323
What I do is
I get stuff organized.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.525
I clear my desktop,
my virtual desktop.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.727
-Your virtual desktop.
-I go on.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.595
I have a couple virtual
online meetings.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:30.729
-Right, love that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:32.332
-"Hey, good to see you man.
How's it going?"

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.267
You know, stuff like that.
My arms are exhausted.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.202
-Oh, my gosh.
-Meeting, meeting, meeting.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.371
And I normally write out actual,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.106
physical thank-you notes
and mail them.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.141
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Do you mail them?

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.776
-Through the U.S.
Postal Service.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.111
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.013
I use our great
U.S. Postal Service.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.548
You know, I wanted to be
a mailman at one point.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.516
-Did you really?
-I really did.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:54.687
I was going into comedy, and my
parents go, "We support you,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.789
but please take
the postal exam."

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:57.923
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:01.494
"See if you -- "
'Cause I loved our mailman.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.895
I loved the idea of it.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.663
I loved that he had
a steering wheel

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:06.566
on the other side of the thing.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.034
He's making his own rules.
-Yeah.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.236
[ Laughter ]
-And wore shorts.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.637
-Yeah.
-Didn't care.

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:12.838
-Walked around.

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:14.073
-Walked around bringing
good news to people.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.375
-Yeah.
-Right? Sometimes bad news.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.743
-One of the greatest services
of all time.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.210
-But he was there
for the ups and downs.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.447
And I'm prepared for that
mentally.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.583
-With them?
-No, with humans.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.618
I could deliver the bills.
I could give you some bad news.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.720
-"Oh, wow, it's a bill, dang."

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.623
Oh, but guess what.
-Guess what. Here's your check.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:34.527
Yeah, or here's a magazine or,
you know, an L.L. Bean catalog.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.195
-Sure.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:39.932
-I'll shove it in the mailbox
with love.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.501
-Yeah. "Life" magazine.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.069
-Yeah, I got four crumpled
L.L. Bean catalogs in here.

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:46.438
-And it was raining outside and
it was wet, so they're soggy.

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:47.940
But guess what.
-There you go. But guess what.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.842
-Still love them.
-Yeah, something to do, right?

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.344
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.045
Gives you something to do. You
go throw it out or recycle it.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.114
-Yeah, or you let it dry,
standing straight up.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.350
-Yeah.
While you're at it, you go,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.652
"Oh, these papers are drying
awfully quick.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.087
There must be a nice draft here.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.622
Maybe I'll get
in the jerky business."

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.590
-Oh, my gosh.
-So, you get thin strips --

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.025
-Sure. Thin strips.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.661
-You know, you lay it out,
whatever that magazine was.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.530
The breeze goes through.
There you go.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.931
You're making yourself
a whole little business.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:14.032
-Delicious jerky. Beef jerky.

00:02:14.032 --> 00:02:15.901
Tuna jerky. Turkey jerky.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.036
I just like saying it --
turkey jerky.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.204
-Yeah, I love saying it too.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.806
And you know who doesn't
get thanks?

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.040
-Who?
-The mailman.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.675
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.611
So next time you're making
jerky, leave some out.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.246
Don't be a jerky and leave
some out for the mailman.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.215
[ Laughter ]
-That's what I'm saying, buddy.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.818
Well, I was running
a bit behind today.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.720
I couldn't write my --
I was just --

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.954
If you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.221
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:37.723
Is that okay with you?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.191
Thank you!

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:42.862
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:46.231
♪♪

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:47.600
-Wow, a lot of 'tude.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.569
-No, he's in a good --
He's in a good mood, man.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:53.406
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.740
♪♪

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.510
Thank you, back-to-school ads,
for really cornering

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.847
the "children jumping
with backpacks" market.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.682
[ Applause ]

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:06.919
Yay!

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.420
♪♪

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.857
Thank you, school,
for being a place where we learn

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.193
new things and make
everlasting friendships.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.862
But mostly get really good
at drawing this thing.

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:21.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.037
♪♪

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:26.739
-I got an eraser. I'm going to
do it with an eraser.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.374
-Let me see if I can do it.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.176
Mm, mm, mm.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.178
Alright, this is the jam.
You start there.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.580
-Yeah, start there.
That's what you start with.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.814
-Alright.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.248
♪♪

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:37.517
-Triangle.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:41.320
-Oh, I do this part I think.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.857
-Oh, I see.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.793
Then you can make kind of
the Celtic cross coming up.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.327
I like that. Yeah.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.030
♪♪

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.799
Ooh!
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.868
Oh, wow, it's like 3-D.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.604
♪♪

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.306
-There you go.
-Wow!

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:07.847
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.449
Yeah, whatever.
-That's what I do, whatever.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.584
I'm at a heavy metal concert,
I'm like --

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.951
-Yeah, alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:14.654
I studied graphic art.
-Let's get it out of the way.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.522
You know?
-Let's get it done.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.390
-Yeah.
-Rock on, sure.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.692
-I want to appreciate the music.
Don't make me perform.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.160
-Yeah. Do you mind sitting down?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.562
Yeah.
Don't stand up in front of me.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.964
-This out of respect,
and let's go.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.133
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.300
♪♪

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.970
-Thank you, old-school
pencil sharpeners,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.472
for being the only part of
my second grader's classroom

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:35.340
that looks like it belongs in
a "Saw" movie.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:41.847
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.582
♪♪

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:47.587
Thank you, Little Caesars
new Crazy Calzony,

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.554
for looking like a board game
where the winner

00:04:49.554 --> 00:04:50.789
gets high blood pressure.

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:56.195
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.698
-It's boiling hot!

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.566
♪♪

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:05.003
-Thank you, mid-August,
or as CVS calls you, Halloween.

00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:07.439
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:08.875
Now?

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.547
♪♪

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.850
Thank you, super-long
auto-generated passwords,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.453
for being a great way
to keep hackers and me

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:24.590
out of my account.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.560
This is a safe one.
I know, I know, I know.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.663
-I got to write it down.
-Password123 is just awesome.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.631
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.233
♪♪

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:38.337
Thank you, people who type "Thx"
instead of "thanks,"

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:40.238
for letting me know
that you're feeling grateful

00:05:40.238 --> 00:05:42.741
but not grateful enough
to type three extra letters.

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:47.246
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.582
Thx but no thx.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.217
-I'm too busy.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.620
♪♪

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.024
-Thank you, coconuts,
for being juicy, tender fruit

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.960
on the inside and porch doormat
on the outside.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.363
There you have it.
Those are our thank-you notes.

